<rss version="2.0" xmlns:atom="http://www.w3.org/2005/Atom" xmlns:media="http://search.yahoo.com/mrss/" xmlns:dc="http://purl.org/dc/elements/1.1/"><channel><language>en</language><title>RFI - All the news from France, Europe, Africa and the rest of the world.</title><description>Follow any political information, cultural, sporting and live streaming on RFI. The latest information, news and events around the world.</description><link>https://www.rfi.fr/en/</link><lastBuildDate>Fri, 17 Jul 2026 07:30:14 GMT</lastBuildDate><atom:link href="https://www.rfi.fr/en/rss" rel="self" type="application/rss+xml"/><item><category>International</category><title>UK Labour party to crown 'King of the North' Burnham as leader and next PM</title><link>https://www.rfi.fr/en/international/20260717-uk-labour-party-crowns-andy-burnham-as-leader-and-next-prime-minister</link><description>
Britain's ruling Labour party will confirm veteran politician Andy Burnham as its new leader, and the country's next prime minister, at a special conference on Friday. He becomes the UK's seventh prime minister in a decade, replacing Keir Starmer.
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.rfi.fr/media/display/7a82cdca-6bd9-11f1-9dde-005056bf30b7/w:1024/p:16x9/000-B7MC6ZR.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.rfi.fr/media/display/7a82cdca-6bd9-11f1-9dde-005056bf30b7/w:1024/p:16x9/000-B7MC6ZR.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">48b66fe4-81ab-11f1-8d4a-213d0dd984d3</guid><pubDate>Fri, 17 Jul 2026 07:17:14 GMT</pubDate><source url="https://s.rfi.fr/media/display/7a82cdca-6bd9-11f1-9dde-005056bf30b7/w:1024/p:16x9/000-B7MC6ZR.jpg">AFP - OLI SCARFF</source><dc:creator>RFI</dc:creator></item><item><category>Africa</category><title>UN campaign trail takes former president Macky Sall back to Senegal</title><link>https://www.rfi.fr/en/africa/20260717-un-campaign-trail-takes-former-president-macky-sall-back-to-senegal</link><description>
Senegal's former president Macky Sall returns home on Friday for the first time since leaving office in April 2024, in a visit tied to his bid to become the next UN secretary-general. But opponents say the violence that marked the final months of his mandate should disqualify him from the role.
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.rfi.fr/media/display/eccf82d0-8103-11f1-bdd1-005056a97e36/w:1024/p:16x9/Macky-sall-UN-SENEGAL-rtrs.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.rfi.fr/media/display/eccf82d0-8103-11f1-bdd1-005056a97e36/w:1024/p:16x9/Macky-sall-UN-SENEGAL-rtrs.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">d6048b00-8102-11f1-a9cf-e51ea97b6ed6</guid><pubDate>Fri, 17 Jul 2026 05:05:14 GMT</pubDate><source url="https://s.rfi.fr/media/display/eccf82d0-8103-11f1-bdd1-005056a97e36/w:1024/p:16x9/Macky-sall-UN-SENEGAL-rtrs.jpg">© REUTERS - Eduardo Munoz </source><dc:creator>RFI</dc:creator></item><item><category>France</category><title>Macron toughens stance on arson, with dozens arrested as wildfires sweep France</title><link>https://www.rfi.fr/en/france/20260716-macron-toughens-stance-on-arson-as-wildfires-sweep-france</link><description>
French President Emmanuel Macron has said there would be "zero tolerance" for arson after France was hit by wildfires that have scorched thousands of hectares, as multiple heatwaves since May have dried out forests and fields. Dozens have been arrested across the country over starting fires, including a volunteer firefighter.  
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.rfi.fr/media/display/52a8fb68-80e1-11f1-bcc5-005056a97e36/w:1024/p:16x9/2026-07-13T182726Z-572366655-RC25DMANXMCE-RTRMADP-3-EUROPE-WEATHER-FRANCE-WILDFIRE.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.rfi.fr/media/display/52a8fb68-80e1-11f1-bcc5-005056a97e36/w:1024/p:16x9/2026-07-13T182726Z-572366655-RC25DMANXMCE-RTRMADP-3-EUROPE-WEATHER-FRANCE-WILDFIRE.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">dbdc550e-8101-11f1-a945-6937b7331399</guid><pubDate>Thu, 16 Jul 2026 12:54:58 GMT</pubDate><source url="https://s.rfi.fr/media/display/52a8fb68-80e1-11f1-bcc5-005056a97e36/w:1024/p:16x9/2026-07-13T182726Z-572366655-RC25DMANXMCE-RTRMADP-3-EUROPE-WEATHER-FRANCE-WILDFIRE.jpg">© Stéphane Mahe/Reuters</source><dc:creator>RFI</dc:creator></item><item><category>France</category><title>Fears over foreign influence in France, as Musk backs Le Pen presidential bid</title><link>https://www.rfi.fr/en/france/20260716-elon-musk-s-backing-of-le-pen-presidential-bid-raises-foreign-influence-concerns-in-france</link><description>
Billionaire Elon Musk has thrown his support behind far-right leader Marine Le Pen's bid for the French presidency, calling her "France's last hope", and prompting accusations of foreign interference in the 2027 election.
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.rfi.fr/media/display/f2c8f552-52ed-11f1-9ea6-005056bfb2b6/w:1024/p:16x9/AP26134407799428.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.rfi.fr/media/display/f2c8f552-52ed-11f1-9ea6-005056bfb2b6/w:1024/p:16x9/AP26134407799428.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">65867bc2-80f8-11f1-aac2-05c808138351</guid><pubDate>Thu, 16 Jul 2026 11:35:21 GMT</pubDate><source url="https://s.rfi.fr/media/display/f2c8f552-52ed-11f1-9ea6-005056bfb2b6/w:1024/p:16x9/AP26134407799428.jpg">© Mark Schiefelbein/AP</source><dc:creator>RFI</dc:creator></item><item><category>France</category><title>French man charged with rape and murder of schoolgirl Lyhanna</title><link>https://www.rfi.fr/en/france/20260716-french-man-charged-with-rape-murder-of-schoolgirl-lyhanna</link><description>
The main suspect in the death of an 11-year-old girl whose body was found in the Gers region has been charged with the rape and murder of a child. The case has sparked nationwide protests and renewed scrutiny of the French justice system, after it emerged that the suspect had previously been accused of raping another child.
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.rfi.fr/media/display/b3b5b03e-7ba2-11f1-ab6b-005056a97e36/w:1024/p:16x9/000-B8PL8KU.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.rfi.fr/media/display/b3b5b03e-7ba2-11f1-ab6b-005056a97e36/w:1024/p:16x9/000-B8PL8KU.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">bf726d0e-80e3-11f1-9ad7-11c429da1086</guid><pubDate>Thu, 16 Jul 2026 06:58:27 GMT</pubDate><source url="https://s.rfi.fr/media/display/b3b5b03e-7ba2-11f1-ab6b-005056a97e36/w:1024/p:16x9/000-B8PL8KU.jpg">© Julie Sebadelha/AFP</source><dc:creator>RFI</dc:creator></item><item><category>Africa</category><title>Greenpeace Africa demands halt to $17bn Kenya coastal oil refinery</title><link>https://www.rfi.fr/en/africa/20260716-greenpeace-demands-halt-to-dangote-s-17bn-kenya-coastal-refinery</link><description>
Climate rights group Greenpeace Africa has called for a halt to a proposed oil refinery project by Africa's richest man, Aliko Dangote, in Kenya's coastal region, warning of the environmental risks. 
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.rfi.fr/media/display/b0ae671c-8027-11f1-8bbc-005056bf30b7/w:1024/p:16x9/000-1HP8JI.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.rfi.fr/media/display/b0ae671c-8027-11f1-8bbc-005056bf30b7/w:1024/p:16x9/000-1HP8JI.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">e4ba7b34-8119-11f1-b689-57e3f657aba9</guid><pubDate>Thu, 16 Jul 2026 13:29:32 GMT</pubDate><source url="https://s.rfi.fr/media/display/b0ae671c-8027-11f1-8bbc-005056bf30b7/w:1024/p:16x9/000-1HP8JI.jpg">AFP - TONY KARUMBA</source><dc:creator>RFI</dc:creator></item><item><category>France</category><title>French parliament passes assisted dying law after years of wrangling</title><link>https://www.rfi.fr/en/france/20260716-france-passes-assisted-dying-law-after-years-of-wrangling</link><description>
France's National Assembly has given its definitive backing to legislation granting terminally ill adults the right to end their lives with medical assistance, bringing to a close a protracted and often fraught political battle.
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.rfi.fr/media/display/49de0e66-807c-11f1-9f6c-005056bf30b7/w:1024/p:16x9/2026-07-15t172906z-1232406278-rc2hemahwno4-rtrmadp-3-france-politics-assisted-dying.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.rfi.fr/media/display/49de0e66-807c-11f1-9f6c-005056bf30b7/w:1024/p:16x9/2026-07-15t172906z-1232406278-rc2hemahwno4-rtrmadp-3-france-politics-assisted-dying.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">af51b17a-807d-11f1-90a2-95c1f2bcc31e</guid><pubDate>Thu, 16 Jul 2026 06:10:19 GMT</pubDate><source url="https://s.rfi.fr/media/display/49de0e66-807c-11f1-9f6c-005056bf30b7/w:1024/p:16x9/2026-07-15t172906z-1232406278-rc2hemahwno4-rtrmadp-3-france-politics-assisted-dying.jpg">© REUTERS/Abdul Saboor</source><dc:creator>RFI</dc:creator></item><item><category>Africa</category><title>Students in Cameroon protest new financial requirements for French visas</title><link>https://www.rfi.fr/en/africa/20260716-cameroonian-students-protest-new-french-visa-financial-rules</link><description>
Dozens of people took to the streets outside the French embassy in Yaoundé this week to protest new rules that require Cameroonian nationals to demonstrate the means to pay tuition fees in full before they can obtain a student visa for France. Protesters say the policy will make studying in France impossible for many people who already have places at French institutions for the coming academic year.
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.rfi.fr/media/display/e54b25f4-8014-11f1-8fc2-005056bfb2b6/w:1024/p:16x9/IMG-5481-1.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.rfi.fr/media/display/e54b25f4-8014-11f1-8fc2-005056bfb2b6/w:1024/p:16x9/IMG-5481-1.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">d7cab886-8028-11f1-95bb-a97de1dfa122</guid><pubDate>Thu, 16 Jul 2026 11:56:25 GMT</pubDate><source url="https://s.rfi.fr/media/display/e54b25f4-8014-11f1-8fc2-005056bfb2b6/w:1024/p:16x9/IMG-5481-1.jpg">© RFI / Emmanuel Jules Ntap</source><dc:creator>RFI</dc:creator></item><item><category>International</category><title>EU and Ukraine seal drone deal to pair industry with battlefield expertise</title><link>https://www.rfi.fr/en/international/20260715-eu-ukraine-agree-drone-deal-to-pair-industry-with-battlefield-expertise</link><description>
European Union chief Ursula von der Leyen on Wednesday announced a drone deal with Ukraine to boost joint production of the key battlefield technology. 
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.rfi.fr/media/display/69785788-8052-11f1-8a0f-005056a90284/w:1024/p:16x9/000-B4UM3WE.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.rfi.fr/media/display/69785788-8052-11f1-8a0f-005056a90284/w:1024/p:16x9/000-B4UM3WE.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">cc56a9b0-8050-11f1-8f9a-192b83c26e62</guid><pubDate>Wed, 15 Jul 2026 18:19:39 GMT</pubDate><source url="https://s.rfi.fr/media/display/69785788-8052-11f1-8a0f-005056a90284/w:1024/p:16x9/000-B4UM3WE.jpg">AFP - GENYA SAVILOV</source><dc:creator>RFI</dc:creator></item><item><category>Africa</category><title>Lawyers vow to fight on after Kenya court rejects Rastafarians' cannabis bid</title><link>https://www.rfi.fr/en/africa/20260716-lawyers-vow-to-fight-on-after-kenya-court-rejects-rastafarians-cannabis-bid</link><description>
In a long-awaited ruling, Kenya's High Court has rejected a bid by Rastafarians to be allowed to smoke cannabis as part of their religious worship. But lawyers say the fight continues and the case has opened up debate on the country's drug laws and what constitutes religious freedom. 
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.rfi.fr/media/display/e35d997e-7f66-11f1-9e5c-005056a90284/w:1024/p:16x9/000-84DG86B.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.rfi.fr/media/display/e35d997e-7f66-11f1-9e5c-005056a90284/w:1024/p:16x9/000-84DG86B.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">69cb1838-802a-11f1-b21e-e9047a96864f</guid><pubDate>Thu, 16 Jul 2026 10:12:12 GMT</pubDate><source url="https://s.rfi.fr/media/display/e35d997e-7f66-11f1-9e5c-005056a90284/w:1024/p:16x9/000-84DG86B.jpg">AFP - SIMON MAINA</source><dc:creator>Alison Hird</dc:creator></item><item><category>France</category><title>Firefighters tackle flare-ups in Fontainebleau forest after reining in blaze</title><link>https://www.rfi.fr/en/france/20260715-firefighters-tackle-flare-ups-in-fontainebleau-forest-after-fires-brought-under-control</link><description>
Around 800 firefighters were still at work in Fontainebleau forest on Wednesday morning, tackling flare-ups after the fires were brought under control the previous day, following 48 hours of intense firefighting.
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.rfi.fr/media/display/3c61ff0c-7fb1-11f1-b6d5-005056bfb2b6/w:1024/p:16x9/000-B9Z39G3.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.rfi.fr/media/display/3c61ff0c-7fb1-11f1-b6d5-005056bfb2b6/w:1024/p:16x9/000-B9Z39G3.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">f11e2794-802a-11f1-977a-e9047a96864f</guid><pubDate>Wed, 15 Jul 2026 11:45:25 GMT</pubDate><source url="https://s.rfi.fr/media/display/3c61ff0c-7fb1-11f1-b6d5-005056bfb2b6/w:1024/p:16x9/000-B9Z39G3.jpg">AFP - FRANCK DESPREZ</source><dc:creator>RFI</dc:creator></item><item><category>Africa</category><title>Ebola cases in DRC may be four times official tally, says WHO</title><link>https://www.rfi.fr/en/africa/20260715-congo-s-ebola-cases-may-be-four-times-official-tally-who-says</link><description>
The true number of Ebola cases in the Democratic Republic of Congo is at least double, and possibly four times, the official tally, the World Health Organization's emergencies chief said on Tuesday. Official figures say the fever has infected nearly 2,000 people since mid-May. 
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.rfi.fr/media/display/0ad2a84a-7f8b-11f1-8951-005056bf30b7/w:1024/p:16x9/2026-07-13-EBOLA-VACCINES-RTRs.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.rfi.fr/media/display/0ad2a84a-7f8b-11f1-8951-005056bf30b7/w:1024/p:16x9/2026-07-13-EBOLA-VACCINES-RTRs.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">c3be3d16-7f8a-11f1-85e1-69386237b861</guid><pubDate>Wed, 15 Jul 2026 14:08:31 GMT</pubDate><source url="https://s.rfi.fr/media/display/0ad2a84a-7f8b-11f1-8951-005056bf30b7/w:1024/p:16x9/2026-07-13-EBOLA-VACCINES-RTRs.jpg">REUTERS - Gradel Muyisa Mumbere</source><dc:creator>RFI</dc:creator></item><item><category>Sports</category><title>Argentina see off England to reach World Cup showdown with Spain</title><link>https://www.rfi.fr/en/sports/20260715-argentina-see-off-england-to-reach-world-cup-final-showdown-with-spain</link><description>
Argentina scored two late goals on Wednesday to eliminate England 2-1 and advance to the 2026 World Cup final against Spain on Sunday. 
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.rfi.fr/media/display/31be05f6-80a5-11f1-bef7-005056bfb2b6/w:1024/p:16x9/laut.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.rfi.fr/media/display/31be05f6-80a5-11f1-bef7-005056bfb2b6/w:1024/p:16x9/laut.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">5b669ae0-80a4-11f1-869e-45cc9bf0894e</guid><pubDate>Wed, 15 Jul 2026 23:44:06 GMT</pubDate><source url="https://s.rfi.fr/media/display/31be05f6-80a5-11f1-bef7-005056bfb2b6/w:1024/p:16x9/laut.jpg">Getty Images via AFP - SHAUN BOTTERILL</source><dc:creator>Paul Myers</dc:creator></item><item><category>International</category><title>United States launches new Iran strikes and reimposes naval blockade</title><link>https://www.rfi.fr/en/international/20260715-us-launches-new-iran-strikes-reimposes-naval-blockade</link><description>
The United States carried out strikes against Iran for a fourth day running on Tuesday and reimposed a naval blockade to prevent ships from sailing to or from the country's ports. 
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.rfi.fr/media/display/720a87ec-7fc9-11f1-884b-005056bfb2b6/w:1024/p:16x9/2026-07-14T131356Z-230358607-RC2PDMA7M9XT-RTRMADP-3-IRAN-CRISIS.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.rfi.fr/media/display/720a87ec-7fc9-11f1-884b-005056bfb2b6/w:1024/p:16x9/2026-07-14T131356Z-230358607-RC2PDMA7M9XT-RTRMADP-3-IRAN-CRISIS.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">b1dc1bf2-8009-11f1-9cfe-d57d8549f440</guid><pubDate>Wed, 15 Jul 2026 05:16:26 GMT</pubDate><source url="https://s.rfi.fr/media/display/720a87ec-7fc9-11f1-884b-005056bfb2b6/w:1024/p:16x9/2026-07-14T131356Z-230358607-RC2PDMA7M9XT-RTRMADP-3-IRAN-CRISIS.jpg">via REUTERS - U.S. Central Command</source><dc:creator>RFI</dc:creator></item><item><category>Sports</category><title>Spain outclass France by 2-0 to advance to World Cup final</title><link>https://www.rfi.fr/en/sports/20260714-spain-outclass-france-to-advance-to-2026-world-cup-final-world-cup-2026</link><description>
Spain produced a masterclass in composure to outwit France 2-0 in Dallas on Tuesday and move into the final of the World Cup, at which they will face either England or Argentina. 
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.rfi.fr/media/display/3ecb1f02-7fd0-11f1-87c0-005056a97e36/w:1024/p:16x9/spain-2.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.rfi.fr/media/display/3ecb1f02-7fd0-11f1-87c0-005056a97e36/w:1024/p:16x9/spain-2.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">6e7b0e22-7fc3-11f1-ad9a-618bd635538c</guid><pubDate>Tue, 14 Jul 2026 22:40:20 GMT</pubDate><source url="https://s.rfi.fr/media/display/3ecb1f02-7fd0-11f1-87c0-005056a97e36/w:1024/p:16x9/spain-2.jpg">AFP - FRANCK FIFE</source><dc:creator>Paul Myers</dc:creator></item><item><category>International</category><title>Gibraltar border checks scrapped in 'new era' following decades of tension</title><link>https://www.rfi.fr/en/international/20260715-gibraltar-and-spain-scrap-border-checks-after-decades-of-tension</link><description>
Border checks were lifted on Wednesday, marking a new era for the tiny British territory's relationship with its Spanish neighbour.
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.rfi.fr/media/display/e651653a-7f65-11f1-b6ac-005056bfb2b6/w:1024/p:16x9/000-B8MR3HT.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.rfi.fr/media/display/e651653a-7f65-11f1-b6ac-005056bfb2b6/w:1024/p:16x9/000-B8MR3HT.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">f8399a58-801c-11f1-98da-79f076fc42a5</guid><pubDate>Wed, 15 Jul 2026 08:59:57 GMT</pubDate><source url="https://s.rfi.fr/media/display/e651653a-7f65-11f1-b6ac-005056bfb2b6/w:1024/p:16x9/000-B8MR3HT.jpg">AFP - JORGE GUERRERO</source><dc:creator>RFI</dc:creator></item><item><category>France</category><title>European troops and planes join Bastille Day parade in show of unity for Ukraine</title><link>https://www.rfi.fr/en/france/20260714-european-troops-and-warplanes-join-paris-military-bastille-day-parade-in-show-of-unity-for-ukraine</link><description>
Some 500 soldiers from the "Coalition of the Willing" backing Ukraine marched down Paris's Champs-Elysees on ​Tuesday in ‌the annual Bastille Day parade, in a showcase of support for Kyiv and a symbolic flexing of European military muscle.
